  (sid, mat_id, 'mcq', 'In a circle with centre \(O\), \(AP\) and \(AQ\) are tangents drawn from an external point \(A\) such that \(\angle PAQ = 90^\circ\). If \(AP = 4\text{ cm}\) then the radius of the circle is', '[{"key": "A", "value": "\\(2\\text{ cm}\\)", "correct": false}, {"key": "B", "value": "\\(3\\text{ cm}\\)", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "\\(4\\text{ cm}\\)", "correct": true}, {"key": "D", "value": "\\(1\\text{ cm}\\)", "correct": false}]', 'C', 1, 'medium', '["Circles"]', '["tangents_radii_angle"]', true),
